#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0467 expect=violation domain=APLB
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when --STDTC is present in a Findings general observation class dataset, where its use is not recommended.
#note "EC-36 AP pin: an Associated Persons dataset carries PARENT-prefixed variables, so APLB holds LBSTDTC (not APLBSTDTC) and --STDTC must resolve to LBSTDTC. Before EC-36 the prefix was the full domain code APLB, the engine looked for APLBSTDTC, found nothing and this rule silently did not fire. ⚠ CLASS-UNREACHABLE IN PRODUCTION, recorded 2026-09-19 (review round 1): CDISC-CG0467 scopes Classes.Include [FINDINGS] - inherited from CORE-000207, which this fixture was MIGRATED from by PLAN-retire-core-family phase 5 - and APLB is in no DomainClassMap family and CustomDomainClassDetector.detectClass finds none of APLBTERM/APLBTRT/APLBQNAM/APLBTESTCD, so the class is NULL and ScopeMatcher.describeClassMismatch is strict-on-null. So DatasetRuleResolver does not emit the rule for this dataset and the scenario cannot fail for the reason it was written. The harness cannot say so: with no class= declaration AbstractRuleTestSuitesFactory.describeScopeMismatch routes the class axis to describeAdamClassMismatch, which deliberately refuses SDTM class scopes and returns null. ⛔ Do NOT delete it - it is now this rule's only APLB coverage and ScenarioFixtureCoverageRatchetTest credits it; the production-reachable pair is the two class=FINDINGS LB fixtures beside it. ⚑ Measured against the OFFLINE class path (DomainClassMap then CustomDomainClassDetector), which is what an unlicensed run and this harness both use; with the CDISC Library reachable the product reverse-walk runs first and may answer differently for a SUPP or AP dataset - it cannot for AE, which is EVENTS on every path."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset APLB label="Associated Persons Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col APID type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
col LBSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col LBSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Observation"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APLB | AP-701-1015 | 1 | 2014-01-03
CDISCPILOT01 | APLB | AP-701-1015 | 2 | 2014-01-09
---
